WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
A doctor presses a grey stick onto a wart.

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.760
Over the next few days, the wart
turns black and breaks down.

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.120
The tip of that stick is a
white solid: silver nitrate.

4
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:16.940
Yet for many years, newborn babies had drops
of silver nitrate put into their eyes,

5
00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.480
to protect them from infection.

6
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:24.880
So how can the same chemical burn away a
wart and protect a newborn baby's eyes?

7
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.800
In this mission, you'll find out
what acids and alkalis do to skin,

8
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.940
and how to deal with a chemical splash.

9
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.760
Then you'll see how corrosive
chemicals remove warts,

10
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.660
and how silver nitrate
attacks living cells.

11
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:42.760
Your mission: explain how one
chemical can do both jobs.